book:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n* 2 tablespoons freshly-[[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] roasted [[Cookbook:Red Pepper|red peppers]], [[Cookbook:Julienne|julienned]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Tomato|sun-dried tomatoes]], julienned\n* ¼ cup pitted Kalamata [[Cookbook:Olive|olives]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Artichoke|artichoke heart]] (canned is fine), cut into 8 pieces\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] dry [[Cookbook:White Wine|white wine]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] [[Cookbook:Broth|broth]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Oregano|dried oregano]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Basil|dried basil]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n* [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|Granulated garlic]], to taste\n* ½ cup fresh [[Cookbook:Broccoli|broccoli florets]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] [[cookbook:Pasta|linguine]], cooked [[Cookbook:Al Dente|al dente]] and drained\n* About ¼ cup crumbled [[Cookbook:Feta Cheese|feta cheese]] for [[Cookbook:Garnish|garnish]]\n* 1–2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]] for garnish\n\n==Procedure==\n# Heat oil in a [[Cookbook:Sauté Pan|sauté pan]] over high heat.\n# Add garlic, and [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sauté]] until it just begins to brown (about 1 minute). Be careful not to burn it.\n# Stir in red peppers, sun-dried tomatoes, olives, and artichoke heart.\n# Add white wine, chicken broth, oregano and basil, and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boil|boil]].\n# Season to taste with salt, pepper and granulated garlic.\n# Add broccoli and cook just until bright green and tender (1–2 minutes).\n# Add pasta and [[Cookbook:Mixing|toss]] to combine.\n# Garnish with crumbled feta cheese and chopped parsley, and serve hot.\n\n[[Category:Italian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using artichoke|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using olive|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes usi